1
00:01:37,239 --> 00:01:38,319
Teaming up with that

2
00:01:38,319 --> 00:01:40,519
girl who ruined your career as a judge...

3
00:01:42,359 --> 00:01:43,840
Are you a masochist,

4
00:01:45,560 --> 00:01:47,359
or just trying to get lucky in your old age?

5
00:01:47,359 --> 00:01:48,359
What did you say? Shut up!

6
00:01:48,359 --> 00:01:49,359
Did you two sleep together?

7
00:01:49,359 --> 00:01:50,680
Shut your filthy mouth!

8
00:01:50,680 --> 00:01:51,760
You're a piece of shit,

9
00:01:51,760 --> 00:01:53,680
but that doesn't mean everyone is as filthy as you!

10
00:01:57,239 --> 00:01:58,519
Try me.

11
00:01:59,480 --> 00:02:00,959
Come on, come on!

12
00:02:01,560 --> 00:02:02,319
Bring it on!

13
00:02:04,239 --> 00:02:06,799
You've finally lost it, Lao Yu.

14
00:02:11,240 --> 00:02:12,120
How does it feel?

15
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:15,719
Feels pretty good, doesn't it?

16
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:16,919
Very amusing.

17
00:02:18,439 --> 00:02:19,439
Let me tell you something.

18
00:02:19,719 --> 00:02:21,879
There's no turning back now.

19
00:02:22,319 --> 00:02:25,520
Do me a favor. Before making any decisions next time,

20
00:02:25,919 --> 00:02:27,319
discuss it with me first.

21
00:02:28,439 --> 00:02:30,560
Don't go acting on your own again.

22
00:02:34,800 --> 00:02:36,000
If you do something stupid again,

23
00:02:37,479 --> 00:02:38,840
I promise I'll show you

24
00:02:39,439 --> 00:02:41,560
what unbearable consequences look like.

25
00:03:35,560 --> 00:03:37,439
I had my own ideals too,

26
00:03:37,439 --> 00:03:38,719
seeking value and meaning

27
00:03:38,719 --> 00:03:39,800
when I joined this profession.

28
00:03:40,960 --> 00:03:42,840
But reality is completely different.

29
00:03:44,120 --> 00:03:45,199
I'm pretty conflicted myself.

30
00:04:17,079 --> 00:04:17,879
Mr. Zhao.

31
00:04:20,759 --> 00:04:21,720
You're still here?

32
00:04:29,800 --> 00:04:30,839
Heading down for a drink?

33
00:04:32,560 --> 00:04:33,759
Thank you for today.

34
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:36,800
It's nothing.

35
00:04:38,920 --> 00:04:39,720
I...

36
00:04:41,360 --> 00:04:42,680
want to take a couple of days off.

37
00:04:42,680 --> 00:04:43,319
No problem.

38
00:04:44,839 --> 00:04:46,000
Take a few extra days to rest.

39
00:04:50,680 --> 00:04:52,120
Once you're fully rested,

40
00:04:52,920 --> 00:04:54,439
you can visit Lao Kang in detention.

41
00:05:03,600 --> 00:05:05,319
As a criminal defense lawyer,

42
00:05:07,439 --> 00:05:09,480
with an organized crime case like this,

43
00:05:10,879 --> 00:05:14,040
it's totally normal to wet your pants.

44
00:05:15,079 --> 00:05:16,040
It's nothing to be ashamed of.

45
00:05:19,120 --> 00:05:21,040
You know, when I first handled these cases,

46
00:05:22,240 --> 00:05:25,319
I'd often get threatened by other gangs.

47
00:05:25,639 --> 00:05:27,639
If you said even one wrong word,

48
00:05:28,959 --> 00:05:31,040
a beating would be getting off easy.

49
00:05:32,040 --> 00:05:34,040
I remember a former colleague

50
00:05:35,199 --> 00:05:37,279
who was slashed over a dozen times.

51
00:05:37,560 --> 00:05:40,040
Luckily, Lao Xu and I got him to the ER in time,

52
00:05:40,560 --> 00:05:42,879
or it would have been a disaster.

53
00:05:44,639 --> 00:05:45,399
But I digress.

54
00:05:46,079 --> 00:05:46,759
Zhou Hao.

55
00:05:47,680 --> 00:05:48,319
Come.

56
00:05:49,680 --> 00:05:51,160
Have a drink and relax.

57
00:05:52,480 --> 00:05:53,240
Come on.

58
00:05:58,079 --> 00:05:58,639
Come on.

59
00:06:08,879 --> 00:06:10,879
You've been pampered since childhood.

60
00:06:12,639 --> 00:06:13,879
I'm sure you have no shortage

61
00:06:13,879 --> 00:06:15,680
of people who say nice things

62
00:06:15,680 --> 00:06:16,879
to comfort you.

63
00:06:17,240 --> 00:06:19,759
But you probably lack someone like me

64
00:06:19,759 --> 00:06:21,439
who can tell you the truth.

65
00:06:28,920 --> 00:06:29,600
Look.

66
00:06:30,360 --> 00:06:31,560
Nice watch.

67
00:06:33,600 --> 00:06:34,600
My dad gave it to me.

68
00:06:35,600 --> 00:06:36,839
As a gift for becoming a lawyer.

69
00:06:41,439 --> 00:06:42,639
I really envy you.

70
00:06:43,560 --> 00:06:44,199
I remember

71
00:06:44,199 --> 00:06:46,279
when I first started out as a lawyer,

72
00:06:46,439 --> 00:06:47,720
I hadn't seen much of the world.

73
00:06:49,399 --> 00:06:52,759
I only knew digital and quartz watches,

74
00:06:54,079 --> 00:06:56,319
or ones you had to wind yourself.

75
00:06:57,839 --> 00:06:58,639
I had no idea

76
00:06:58,639 --> 00:07:00,920
there were six-figure mechanical watches

77
00:07:01,439 --> 00:07:03,560
with an automatic winding function.

78
00:07:11,959 --> 00:07:13,920
Do you know why I'm telling you this?

79
00:07:16,160 --> 00:07:17,360
I don't want to rely on my dad.

80
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:20,199
I've always worked hard.

81
00:07:21,720 --> 00:07:24,519
Right, worked hard.

82
00:07:26,160 --> 00:07:29,360
Kids who grew up in your environment

83
00:07:31,120 --> 00:07:32,839
are all spoiled.

84
00:07:33,240 --> 00:07:35,040
Because you're always surrounded by people

85
00:07:35,040 --> 00:07:36,040
who flatter you,

86
00:07:36,800 --> 00:07:38,040
protect you,

87
00:07:38,439 --> 00:07:39,399
and coddle you.

88
00:07:40,319 --> 00:07:41,319
So you think

89
00:07:41,319 --> 00:07:43,680
that with just a tiny bit of effort,

90
00:07:43,959 --> 00:07:45,160
you deserve all that

91
00:07:45,160 --> 00:07:47,439
applause, flowers, and success.

92
00:07:49,079 --> 00:07:50,360
Because you're used to it.

93
00:07:52,560 --> 00:07:54,079
But like people who wear digital watches

94
00:07:54,079 --> 00:07:56,040
and those who wear mechanical ones,

95
00:07:56,439 --> 00:07:59,399
they are blind to each other's worlds.

96
00:08:00,800 --> 00:08:01,920
Look at you today.

97
00:08:03,079 --> 00:08:03,759
When you are forced to

98
00:08:03,759 --> 00:08:07,240
face confusion and the unknown,

99
00:08:08,399 --> 00:08:10,439
your true colors show.

100
00:08:14,399 --> 00:08:15,560
All that's left is fear,

101
00:08:16,240 --> 00:08:19,720
wondering if you should just surrender.

102
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:24,160
In this life,

103
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:27,360
people do a lot to deceive themselves.

104
00:08:28,160 --> 00:08:29,240
In your eyes,

105
00:08:29,319 --> 00:08:30,360
you think being a lawyer,

106
00:08:30,360 --> 00:08:32,080
fighting to the bitter end, is cool.

107
00:08:33,559 --> 00:08:36,600
Taking the moral high ground is cool.

108
00:08:37,240 --> 00:08:38,679
Not relying on your dad is even cooler.

109
00:08:38,679 --> 00:08:39,639
It's not vanity.

110
00:08:41,399 --> 00:08:42,519
It's not vanity.

111
00:08:46,240 --> 00:08:49,840
Being a defense lawyer has meaning.

112
00:08:52,360 --> 00:08:53,120
It's not vanity.

113
00:08:54,320 --> 00:08:54,960
Right.

114
00:08:57,399 --> 00:09:00,519
You wear a six-figure watch.

115
00:09:01,879 --> 00:09:04,360
How often do you check it for the time?

116
00:09:07,879 --> 00:09:10,399
Don't you still rely on your phone?

117
00:09:11,240 --> 00:09:12,600
The "meaning" you speak of

118
00:09:13,600 --> 00:09:16,320
is just packaging to make you feel better.

119
00:09:18,240 --> 00:09:19,639
If you threw this watch away right now,

120
00:09:20,919 --> 00:09:22,679
wouldn't you still live just fine?

121
00:09:29,679 --> 00:09:31,039
It's not vanity.

122
00:09:35,720 --> 00:09:37,360
But that female assistant of yours

123
00:09:39,639 --> 00:09:40,960
is different from you.

124
00:09:41,600 --> 00:09:43,799
Without pain and fear,

125
00:09:48,200 --> 00:09:49,879
she couldn't survive.

126
00:09:54,360 --> 00:09:55,080
Zhou Hao,

127
00:09:56,440 --> 00:09:57,279
"meaning"

128
00:09:57,600 --> 00:09:59,279
isn't just the icing on the cake.

129
00:09:59,799 --> 00:10:01,279
Only when you truly feel

130
00:10:01,279 --> 00:10:03,240
that it's your reason for living

131
00:10:03,480 --> 00:10:06,879
does meaning have any value.

132
00:10:12,440 --> 00:10:13,159
Mr. Zhao,

133
00:10:14,600 --> 00:10:15,399
right now,

134
00:10:17,919 --> 00:10:19,399
my mind is a mess.

135
00:10:22,440 --> 00:10:23,759
Lao Kang has injuries.

136
00:10:25,440 --> 00:10:26,399
He was beaten.

137
00:10:27,559 --> 00:10:29,000
It might be a forced confession.

138
00:10:29,000 --> 00:10:29,679
Zhou Hao.

139
00:10:31,600 --> 00:10:33,399
I've already said so much to you.

140
00:10:33,559 --> 00:10:35,799
Don't make me feel I'm wasting my breath.

141
00:10:35,799 --> 00:10:36,519
Okay?

142
00:10:40,679 --> 00:10:42,200
I'll ask you one last time.

143
00:10:43,720 --> 00:10:45,480
Plead guilty and accept the penalty,

144
00:10:47,759 --> 00:10:49,600
or fight for an acquittal?

145
00:10:58,080 --> 00:10:59,039
Plead guilty.

146
00:11:05,279 --> 00:11:06,960
I agree with Lawyer Zhou.

147
00:11:12,240 --> 00:11:13,200
Let's do that.

148
00:11:35,120 --> 00:11:35,879
Where's Zhou Hao?

149
00:11:47,200 --> 00:11:48,000
The reason.

150
00:11:50,159 --> 00:11:51,600
I explained it to you on the phone.

151
00:11:52,080 --> 00:11:53,440
A family member got sick that day,

152
00:11:53,559 --> 00:11:54,919
so I didn't go to the detention center,

153
00:11:55,039 --> 00:11:55,960
and went straight home.

154
00:11:56,080 --> 00:11:58,480
I don't mean why you went missing.

155
00:11:58,960 --> 00:11:59,559
I mean

156
00:11:59,559 --> 00:12:01,519
the reason for the sudden guilty plea.

157
00:12:02,879 --> 00:12:04,080
Lao Kang pleaded guilty.

158
00:12:05,320 --> 00:12:07,080
We have to respect the client's wishes.

159
00:12:08,720 --> 00:12:09,320
Oh, really?

160
00:12:10,039 --> 00:12:11,559
Have you seen Lao Kang in detention?

161
00:12:12,559 --> 00:12:13,279
Are you sure

162
00:12:13,279 --> 00:12:15,399
pleading guilty is what Lao Kang wants?

163
00:12:15,600 --> 00:12:16,519
Then what about those obvious

164
00:12:16,519 --> 00:12:17,799
loopholes in the evidence?

165
00:12:17,799 --> 00:12:20,200
Can you stop being so aggressive?

166
00:12:20,799 --> 00:12:23,480
I asked you here to help me.

167
00:12:24,279 --> 00:12:26,039
What, you won't listen to me now?

168
00:12:26,360 --> 00:12:27,200
Listen to you?

169
00:12:27,240 --> 00:12:29,000
Yes, listen to me.

170
00:12:30,679 --> 00:12:31,799
For Lao Kang's case,

171
00:12:31,919 --> 00:12:33,759
the client has already pleaded guilty.

172
00:12:34,320 --> 00:12:35,360
As defense lawyers,

173
00:12:35,360 --> 00:12:37,240
we should respect the client's wishes.

174
00:12:38,080 --> 00:12:39,399
Why are you refusing to let this go?

175
00:12:39,399 --> 00:12:41,200
Are you trying to steal my spotlight?

176
00:12:41,200 --> 00:12:41,960
Come on.

177
00:12:42,600 --> 00:12:44,000
Or do you want to use this case

178
00:12:44,000 --> 00:12:45,120
to get into Rujie directly?

179
00:12:45,320 --> 00:12:46,440
Getting into Rujie is easy.

180
00:12:46,440 --> 00:12:47,519
I can put in a good word for you.

181
00:12:47,679 --> 00:12:48,320
But at the very least,

182
00:12:48,320 --> 00:12:50,039
wait until I've secured my footing there.

183
00:12:50,559 --> 00:12:51,840
What are you talking about?

184
00:12:55,120 --> 00:12:55,919
Zhou Hao.

185
00:12:57,080 --> 00:12:58,159
Did someone pressure you

186
00:12:58,159 --> 00:12:59,559
to change the litigation strategy?

187
00:12:59,559 --> 00:13:00,399
No.

188
00:13:00,679 --> 00:13:01,720
No, Ding Ning.

189
00:13:01,720 --> 00:13:02,519
Stop spending all your time

190
00:13:02,519 --> 00:13:03,879
making up imaginary enemies for yourself.

191
00:13:03,879 --> 00:13:05,080
There aren't that many enemies out there.

192
00:13:05,080 --> 00:13:06,320
Not everyone is like you,

193
00:13:06,320 --> 00:13:08,440
wanting to take on the whole world.

194
00:13:12,600 --> 00:13:14,000
With the nursing home case,

195
00:13:14,200 --> 00:13:15,799
haven't you learned your lesson?

196
00:13:16,559 --> 00:13:17,399
I get it.

197
00:13:18,120 --> 00:13:20,600
Xu Ruqing is handling the bribery charge.

198
00:13:20,799 --> 00:13:21,799
Did Xu Ruqing say something to you?

199
00:13:21,799 --> 00:13:22,600
Just because you have a father

200
00:13:22,600 --> 00:13:23,960
who you think was wrongfully accused,

201
00:13:23,960 --> 00:13:25,080
you habitually assume

202
00:13:25,080 --> 00:13:27,000
that all your clients are innocent.

203
00:13:27,080 --> 00:13:28,279
Meanwhile, you push everyone around you

204
00:13:28,279 --> 00:13:29,519
into a corner.

205
00:13:35,320 --> 00:13:36,000
Is that so?

206
00:13:47,799 --> 00:13:48,799
Nobody owes you anything.

207
00:14:11,639 --> 00:14:12,399
Is this Ding Ning?

208
00:14:12,840 --> 00:14:13,559
Who's calling?

209
00:14:13,960 --> 00:14:15,519
Hello, this is Zhao Yijie.

210
00:14:17,440 --> 00:14:18,840
Yang Awu's adoptive father.

211
00:14:19,559 --> 00:14:20,879
The actual client in Lao Kang's case.

212
00:14:21,759 --> 00:14:22,519
Your phone number...

213
00:14:22,519 --> 00:14:24,519
I had to beg Lao Yu for it.

214
00:14:24,679 --> 00:14:27,279
Sorry if I'm being presumptuous.

215
00:14:27,559 --> 00:14:28,279
It's fine.

216
00:14:28,679 --> 00:14:30,440
I'm calling because...

217
00:14:32,039 --> 00:14:33,039
How should I put this?

218
00:14:34,320 --> 00:14:35,399
I'm a lawyer too.

219
00:14:36,240 --> 00:14:37,120
So I know that

220
00:14:37,919 --> 00:14:39,240
a client's family

221
00:14:39,600 --> 00:14:42,639
shouldn't interfere with case strategy.

222
00:14:43,600 --> 00:14:44,799
But Zhou Hao

223
00:14:46,080 --> 00:14:47,840
has really gone a bit off track.

224
00:14:48,480 --> 00:14:49,519
Anyway, I find

225
00:14:49,639 --> 00:14:51,480
the idea of having Lao Kang plead guilty

226
00:14:51,960 --> 00:14:52,960
a bit hard to accept.

227
00:14:54,279 --> 00:14:56,159
I can't tell Zhou Hao directly,

228
00:14:57,039 --> 00:14:58,720
because I'm his boss, after all.

229
00:15:00,000 --> 00:15:00,799
Plus...

230
00:15:03,320 --> 00:15:04,120
How about this?

231
00:15:05,080 --> 00:15:06,799
I just got back from a business trip.

232
00:15:06,799 --> 00:15:09,799
I'm going to Lao Yu's to pick up Yang Awu.

233
00:15:09,960 --> 00:15:11,639
Would you like to have dinner with us?

234
00:15:11,919 --> 00:15:13,240
Right at Lao Yu's place.

235
00:15:13,879 --> 00:15:14,840
At Lao Yu's?

236
00:15:16,799 --> 00:15:19,039
Lao Yu and I have been friends for years.

237
00:15:19,600 --> 00:15:20,840
We talk about almost everything.

238
00:15:22,200 --> 00:15:23,399
That you're staying at his place,

239
00:15:24,559 --> 00:15:26,080
both Awu and Lao Yu

240
00:15:26,799 --> 00:15:27,919
told me about it long ago.

241
00:15:28,919 --> 00:15:30,279
So you don't need to avoid me.

242
00:15:31,039 --> 00:15:32,360
You're heading home anyway.

243
00:15:33,440 --> 00:15:34,480
Lao Yu...

244
00:15:35,039 --> 00:15:36,399
has recently been treating Yang Awu

245
00:15:36,399 --> 00:15:37,960
like his own child.

246
00:15:38,279 --> 00:15:39,720
Once I pick him up today,

247
00:15:39,919 --> 00:15:41,320
Lao Yu will have to go back

248
00:15:41,320 --> 00:15:42,799
to living all by himself again.

249
00:15:43,279 --> 00:15:44,360
So,

250
00:15:45,039 --> 00:15:46,759
I think he might need you there.

251
00:15:51,240 --> 00:15:52,039
What do you think?

252
00:16:06,000 --> 00:16:06,799
See you at dinner.

253
00:16:08,480 --> 00:16:10,879
Okay, see you at dinner.

254
00:16:43,759 --> 00:16:44,399
Who is it?

255
00:16:45,440 --> 00:16:46,279
I'm back.

256
00:16:49,080 --> 00:16:50,000
Didn't I tell you

257
00:16:50,000 --> 00:16:52,279
to stay at a hotel and not come back?

258
00:16:52,919 --> 00:16:54,399
Didn't you get my text?

259
00:16:54,799 --> 00:16:55,320
Is that so?

260
00:16:55,320 --> 00:16:56,000
Ding Ning.

261
00:16:56,320 --> 00:16:56,960
Awu.

262
00:16:58,159 --> 00:16:59,240
I didn't check my phone.

263
00:17:01,600 --> 00:17:03,200
Even though I have Alzheimer's,

264
00:17:03,200 --> 00:17:05,119
I used to be a judge, you know.

265
00:17:05,119 --> 00:17:07,359
I can tell when someone's lying.

266
00:17:08,079 --> 00:17:08,759
Alright.

267
00:17:09,920 --> 00:17:11,200
I need to see Zhao Yijie.

268
00:17:11,359 --> 00:17:12,640
Why do you need to see him?

269
00:17:13,359 --> 00:17:14,799
Zhou Hao is unreliable.

270
00:17:14,880 --> 00:17:17,000
I need to win over Lao Kang's real client,

271
00:17:17,000 --> 00:17:18,880
which is Zhao Yijie himself,

272
00:17:18,960 --> 00:17:21,000
so I can switch to a not-guilty plea.

273
00:17:21,000 --> 00:17:22,440
I know. I get it.

274
00:17:23,000 --> 00:17:25,079
But I really don't want people gossiping.

275
00:17:25,559 --> 00:17:26,440
You know?

276
00:17:26,839 --> 00:17:27,880
Didn't you already tell them

277
00:17:27,880 --> 00:17:28,799
that I'm staying at your place?

278
00:17:29,880 --> 00:17:30,400
But...

279
00:17:50,799 --> 00:17:52,279
Hello, little guy.

280
00:17:54,200 --> 00:17:55,160
Don't run.

281
00:18:03,400 --> 00:18:04,319
We finally meet.

282
00:18:13,720 --> 00:18:15,279
Ning, come give me a hand.

283
00:18:18,079 --> 00:18:18,799
Zhao Yijie.

284
00:18:22,079 --> 00:18:22,640
Ding Ning.

285
00:18:23,200 --> 00:18:23,839
Hello.

286
00:18:27,440 --> 00:18:28,000
Here, this is for you.

287
00:18:28,000 --> 00:18:28,720
Come on, Ding Ning.

288
00:18:29,319 --> 00:18:30,079
Awu.

289
00:18:30,759 --> 00:18:32,039
Awu, do you want this?

290
00:18:32,039 --> 00:18:32,799
Go on, Awu.

291
00:18:32,960 --> 00:18:33,559
Do you want it?

292
00:18:33,559 --> 00:18:34,599
Play by yourself for a bit.

293
00:18:36,440 --> 00:18:38,160
Awu, it's dangerous here in the kitchen.

294
00:18:38,240 --> 00:18:39,200
Go sit on the couch for now.

295
00:18:39,200 --> 00:18:40,039
No, it's fine.

296
00:18:40,039 --> 00:18:41,680
It's more dangerous outside, right?

297
00:18:42,160 --> 00:18:43,000
What do you want to eat?

298
00:18:43,359 --> 00:18:44,359
We have... we have noodles.

299
00:18:44,519 --> 00:18:45,440
I'll get you a bowl.

300
00:18:45,680 --> 00:18:46,079
Okay.

301
00:18:48,839 --> 00:18:50,200
You like noodles, don't you?

302
00:18:50,599 --> 00:18:51,920
You're in for a treat with Grandpa.

303
00:18:58,599 --> 00:18:59,599
It tastes pretty good.

304
00:18:59,599 --> 00:19:00,759
But a bit bland.

305
00:19:06,039 --> 00:19:07,200
Want some vinegar?

306
00:19:24,039 --> 00:19:26,359
Awu, come have some shrimp.

307
00:19:29,359 --> 00:19:30,640
You won't even eat shrimp?

308
00:19:30,960 --> 00:19:32,119
Are you feeling unwell?

309
00:19:32,640 --> 00:19:34,319
I shouldn't have taken you to the hospital.

310
00:19:36,960 --> 00:19:38,960
The last time I had a home-cooked meal

311
00:19:39,200 --> 00:19:40,400
was probably half a year ago.

312
00:19:40,400 --> 00:19:43,200
These are all pre-packaged and takeout.

313
00:19:43,799 --> 00:19:44,920
Anyone with hands can make them.

314
00:19:44,920 --> 00:19:46,480
Don't be so dramatic, okay?

315
00:19:46,759 --> 00:19:49,039
A home-cooked meal isn't about the food.

316
00:19:49,319 --> 00:19:51,240
It's the home, right?

317
00:19:52,559 --> 00:19:54,799
I think the four of us sitting here eating

318
00:19:55,759 --> 00:19:57,079
feels a lot like a family.

319
00:19:58,000 --> 00:19:59,119
Feels like a courtroom.

320
00:19:59,319 --> 00:20:00,960
One judge, two lawyers.

321
00:20:06,640 --> 00:20:07,759
How did you two meet?

322
00:20:08,240 --> 00:20:09,000
Us two?

323
00:20:11,000 --> 00:20:12,519
Lao Yu and I were in a case together.

324
00:20:13,839 --> 00:20:15,400
But back then he wasn't a judge.

325
00:20:15,920 --> 00:20:17,039
He was the victim's family.

326
00:20:19,480 --> 00:20:21,319
Was it Mr. Yu's wife and son?

327
00:20:21,319 --> 00:20:23,319
Yes, I was the lawyer for the second trial.

328
00:20:26,799 --> 00:20:27,759
Speaking of which,

329
00:20:30,000 --> 00:20:31,960
I've actually always felt regret over it.

330
00:20:32,519 --> 00:20:34,440
Although I never met Mr. Yu's son,

331
00:20:34,880 --> 00:20:35,880
I heard he was,

332
00:20:36,440 --> 00:20:37,319
just like our Awu,

333
00:20:37,319 --> 00:20:38,720
smart and lively.

334
00:20:40,839 --> 00:20:43,079
And he really liked math, right?

335
00:20:48,359 --> 00:20:49,240
He was good at sports too.

336
00:20:49,599 --> 00:20:50,680
He played basketball exceptionally well.

337
00:20:50,680 --> 00:20:52,960
Because I signed a letter of forgiveness,

338
00:20:52,960 --> 00:20:54,559
I didn't have to attend the second trial.

339
00:20:54,960 --> 00:20:57,000
I never even met you back then.

340
00:20:57,400 --> 00:20:59,599
You seem to know my family pretty well.

341
00:21:01,240 --> 00:21:02,000
Well, I'm a lawyer.

342
00:21:04,720 --> 00:21:07,359
But later, we wished we'd met sooner.

343
00:21:12,200 --> 00:21:12,960
What about you two?

344
00:21:19,079 --> 00:21:20,480
Also because of a case.

345
00:21:20,960 --> 00:21:23,480
So because of this case, you two...

346
00:21:27,839 --> 00:21:30,079
What... what are you thinking?

347
00:21:31,160 --> 00:21:33,200
Why keep bringing up the past?

348
00:21:33,960 --> 00:21:35,319
Does it help with digestion?

349
00:21:37,240 --> 00:21:40,359
I'm not bringing this up to be sad.

350
00:21:40,640 --> 00:21:42,720
It's because I feel that

351
00:21:42,720 --> 00:21:44,799
the four of us sitting here eating

352
00:21:45,279 --> 00:21:46,000
should be grateful.

353
00:21:46,000 --> 00:21:48,759
We've let go of superficial rivalries

354
00:21:49,240 --> 00:21:51,960
to find similarities in our souls.

355
00:21:52,359 --> 00:21:53,200
Souls?

356
00:21:54,400 --> 00:21:56,079
Have you ever seen one?

357
00:21:56,720 --> 00:21:57,640
I guess not.

358
00:22:04,400 --> 00:22:05,839
I feel like with you, I also have this

359
00:22:06,119 --> 00:22:07,400
feeling that we should've met sooner.

360
00:22:14,400 --> 00:22:16,119
Actually, about Zhou Hao's case...

361
00:22:16,440 --> 00:22:17,160
Awu,

362
00:22:17,680 --> 00:22:18,480
are you full?

363
00:22:19,400 --> 00:22:21,119
If you're full, go back to your room and play.

364
00:22:22,079 --> 00:22:22,720
Go on.

365
00:22:30,559 --> 00:22:31,519
Ding Ning, here's the thing.

366
00:22:32,559 --> 00:22:33,279
Before that,

367
00:22:33,279 --> 00:22:35,680
I'd like to discuss Xu Ruqing's case.

368
00:22:35,880 --> 00:22:36,519
Is that okay?

369
00:22:37,400 --> 00:22:38,880
Compared to Xu Ruqing's case,

370
00:22:39,440 --> 00:22:41,640
I'd rather hear what happened to Zhou Hao.

371
00:22:44,559 --> 00:22:47,640
As the client for Lao Kang's case,

372
00:22:48,160 --> 00:22:50,680
I want to get a general understanding

373
00:22:51,279 --> 00:22:52,440
of Lawyer Ding's abilities first.

374
00:22:52,720 --> 00:22:53,839
By talking about one case?

375
00:22:54,640 --> 00:22:55,519
Talking about one case

376
00:22:55,519 --> 00:22:57,880
might not be enough to prove my skills.

377
00:22:58,119 --> 00:22:59,359
So you're saying...

378
00:22:59,559 --> 00:23:01,880
Ding Ning, is that pot of soup ready?

379
00:23:02,119 --> 00:23:03,200
The soup you were making.

380
00:23:12,680 --> 00:23:14,160
What are you doing? What do you want?

381
00:23:14,359 --> 00:23:16,279
This is my home, not an office.

382
00:23:16,359 --> 00:23:18,440
Who are you interviewing here?

383
00:23:18,440 --> 00:23:20,039
We're just chatting.

384
00:23:20,039 --> 00:23:21,240
What's there to chat about?

385
00:23:21,240 --> 00:23:22,759
She's just an assistant lawyer.

386
00:23:22,799 --> 00:23:25,400
Don't turn her into another Zhou Hao.

387
00:23:26,000 --> 00:23:27,599
I know what you're plotting.

388
00:23:29,119 --> 00:23:29,839
Alright.

389
00:23:32,559 --> 00:23:33,279
Let me do it.

390
00:23:45,519 --> 00:23:46,200
Okay, thanks.

391
00:23:47,359 --> 00:23:49,240
So, what do you think of the legal profession?

392
00:23:49,480 --> 00:23:52,440
Why do you always chat at the table?

393
00:23:52,440 --> 00:23:53,839
Didn't your mother teach you?

394
00:23:53,839 --> 00:23:55,519
No talking during meals or in bed.

395
00:23:55,559 --> 00:23:57,279
It's basic manners.

396
00:23:57,279 --> 00:23:59,599
We're all gathered here to eat.

397
00:23:59,880 --> 00:24:01,559
Isn't it awkward if no one talks?

398
00:24:02,240 --> 00:24:03,160
It is pretty awkward.

399
00:24:03,160 --> 00:24:03,680
Right.

400
00:24:04,359 --> 00:24:05,559
Look, Lao Yu.

401
00:24:05,599 --> 00:24:06,839
Let me ask you a question, okay?

402
00:24:07,640 --> 00:24:09,519
You've been a judge for most of your life.

403
00:24:09,559 --> 00:24:11,680
Haven't you ever felt...

404
00:24:12,680 --> 00:24:13,359
Felt what?

405
00:24:13,480 --> 00:24:15,079
Anyway, I've been a lawyer for so many years.

406
00:24:15,519 --> 00:24:17,200
I've long grown tired of many things.

407
00:24:17,200 --> 00:24:18,400
I've long been numb to them.

408
00:24:19,119 --> 00:24:20,559
I just wanted to ask Ding Ning.

409
00:24:20,559 --> 00:24:22,319
Is she different from the two of us?

410
00:24:22,640 --> 00:24:24,119
Who would be like you?

411
00:24:25,400 --> 00:24:26,079
It's fine.

412
00:24:26,680 --> 00:24:27,960
Ask whatever you want.

413
00:24:37,559 --> 00:24:39,240
I often wonder to myself...

414
00:24:40,039 --> 00:24:41,759
I just want to figure out...

415
00:24:41,759 --> 00:24:43,880
exactly when did I start...

416
00:24:44,400 --> 00:24:46,440
getting addicted to the legal profession?

417
00:24:48,000 --> 00:24:49,119
You might say it's for money.

418
00:24:50,279 --> 00:24:51,039
It's not.

419
00:24:52,119 --> 00:24:53,559
For people with brains like ours,

420
00:24:54,079 --> 00:24:55,839
going into finance or starting a business

421
00:24:55,839 --> 00:24:56,799
would definitely earn more.

422
00:24:58,920 --> 00:25:00,200
For power, then?

423
00:25:00,640 --> 00:25:01,599
That's even less likely.

424
00:25:02,400 --> 00:25:04,440
Taking crap from judges every day,

425
00:25:04,799 --> 00:25:06,079
taking crap from prosecutors...

426
00:25:06,079 --> 00:25:07,640
what power is there to speak of?

427
00:25:08,839 --> 00:25:10,519
And it definitely isn't for the clients.

428
00:25:11,319 --> 00:25:12,880
Clients are the craziest of all.

429
00:25:14,960 --> 00:25:15,920
So, in the very beginning,

430
00:25:15,920 --> 00:25:18,559
there must have been some kind of joy.

431
00:25:20,039 --> 00:25:22,480
But what is this joy?

432
00:25:26,000 --> 00:25:26,839
Definition.

433
00:25:27,400 --> 00:25:29,200
What? Definition?

434
00:25:30,519 --> 00:25:33,359
Right. The joy of definition.

435
00:25:34,519 --> 00:25:35,759
At least for me,

436
00:25:36,000 --> 00:25:38,039
being a lawyer is like doing research.

437
00:25:38,559 --> 00:25:39,759
It is a form of creation.

438
00:25:39,880 --> 00:25:40,839
Creation?

439
00:25:42,200 --> 00:25:44,079
Discovering patterns in nature,

440
00:25:44,079 --> 00:25:45,400
and defining those patterns.

441
00:25:45,960 --> 00:25:47,680
That in itself is a form of creation.

442
00:25:48,279 --> 00:25:49,279
I get it.

443
00:25:49,759 --> 00:25:51,400
Just like mathematics.

444
00:25:54,680 --> 00:25:57,319
It's a language of creation itself, right?

445
00:25:57,839 --> 00:25:58,519
Exactly.

446
00:26:00,960 --> 00:26:03,599
Literature uses words to map the world.

447
00:26:04,079 --> 00:26:05,240
The difference between math and words

448
00:26:05,240 --> 00:26:06,559
is that math uses numbers.

449
00:26:07,000 --> 00:26:08,680
But fundamentally, they are the same.

450
00:26:09,119 --> 00:26:11,720
They both create something out of nothing,

451
00:26:11,839 --> 00:26:13,599
bridging the gap between us and the world.

452
00:26:15,839 --> 00:26:18,160
What's this got to do with being a lawyer?

453
00:26:21,839 --> 00:26:23,440
In a lawyer's world,

454
00:26:24,160 --> 00:26:25,799
what we face is ambiguity,

455
00:26:25,799 --> 00:26:28,680
gray areas, complexity, and disorder.

456
00:26:28,880 --> 00:26:30,880
But only through definition

457
00:26:30,880 --> 00:26:31,960
can we capture it.

458
00:26:32,680 --> 00:26:34,759
Like defining someone's actions, motives,

459
00:26:34,759 --> 00:26:35,680
or even consequences,

460
00:26:36,079 --> 00:26:38,039
finding that often elusive

461
00:26:38,039 --> 00:26:39,400
corresponding law.

462
00:26:40,160 --> 00:26:42,640
Only then can order and simplicity return.

463
00:26:43,400 --> 00:26:44,559
And a sense of order,

464
00:26:44,960 --> 00:26:47,440
to some extent, is a sense of security.

465
00:26:48,000 --> 00:26:49,799
So every messy case

466
00:26:50,279 --> 00:26:52,200
is like a wild beast waiting to be tamed.

467
00:26:53,839 --> 00:26:56,799
Perhaps that is the joy of it.

468
00:26:59,480 --> 00:27:00,359
Brilliant.

469
00:27:04,680 --> 00:27:06,480
Alright, I'm done eating.

470
00:27:06,720 --> 00:27:07,480
Thank you all.

471
00:27:08,359 --> 00:27:10,000
It's Tuesday, I have a meeting tonight.

472
00:27:10,000 --> 00:27:10,960
I have to go now.

473
00:27:12,279 --> 00:27:13,119
Awu,

474
00:27:13,240 --> 00:27:14,440
let's go home with Dad.

475
00:27:14,920 --> 00:27:16,240
Let Awu stay here.

476
00:27:19,480 --> 00:27:20,839
Awu is feeling a bit unwell.

477
00:27:20,839 --> 00:27:22,160
Didn't you say you were busy

478
00:27:22,160 --> 00:27:23,599
with some regular meeting?

479
00:27:23,599 --> 00:27:25,279
Don't make him run back and forth.

480
00:27:25,279 --> 00:27:27,920
You can't take care of him anyway, right?

481
00:27:29,039 --> 00:27:30,480
Alright, let's not put him through that.

482
00:27:30,960 --> 00:27:32,920
I'll pick him up in a few days. Okay?

483
00:27:33,359 --> 00:27:34,000
Okay.

484
00:27:36,480 --> 00:27:37,400
I'll see you out.

485
00:27:43,039 --> 00:27:44,200
As for Lao Kang's case,

486
00:27:44,200 --> 00:27:45,319
come to my law firm tomorrow,

487
00:27:45,680 --> 00:27:46,480
and we'll discuss it in detail.

488
00:27:47,880 --> 00:27:48,720
Tomorrow?

489
00:27:49,079 --> 00:27:49,960
See you tomorrow.

490
00:27:58,839 --> 00:28:00,319
After deliberation by the collegial panel,

491
00:28:00,319 --> 00:28:02,119
in defendant Kang Qingsong's robbery case,

492
00:28:02,119 --> 00:28:04,440
the facts are clear, the evidence solid.

493
00:28:04,680 --> 00:28:07,200
The court now renders its judgment:

494
00:28:07,720 --> 00:28:08,599
All rise.

495
00:28:13,440 --> 00:28:14,720
Defendant Kang Qingsong

496
00:28:14,839 --> 00:28:15,960
is found guilty of robbery

497
00:28:15,960 --> 00:28:18,279
and sentenced to four and a half years,

498
00:28:18,480 --> 00:28:20,599
along with a fine of 5,000 RMB.

499
00:28:21,279 --> 00:28:23,000
He is guilty of illegal firearm possession

500
00:28:23,079 --> 00:28:25,240
and sentenced to two and a half years.

501
00:28:25,599 --> 00:28:26,599
For the combined offenses,

502
00:28:26,839 --> 00:28:29,119
he shall serve a total of six years,

503
00:28:29,200 --> 00:28:31,319
along with a fine of 5,000 RMB.

504
00:28:31,519 --> 00:28:32,799
If you do not accept this judgment,

505
00:28:32,920 --> 00:28:33,759
after receiving the written judgment...

506
00:28:33,759 --> 00:28:34,359
Are you sure

507
00:28:34,359 --> 00:28:36,480
pleading guilty is what Lao Kang wants?

508
00:28:36,680 --> 00:28:37,720
Then what about those

509
00:28:37,720 --> 00:28:38,759
obvious loopholes in the evidence?

510
00:28:38,920 --> 00:28:39,799
The accomplice's testimony,

511
00:28:40,039 --> 00:28:40,799
the gun's serial number,

512
00:28:40,799 --> 00:28:42,079
and the bullet evidence all match up.

513
00:28:42,759 --> 00:28:43,960
He also pleaded guilty himself.

514
00:28:44,440 --> 00:28:45,559
Do you still want to overturn his case?

515
00:28:46,240 --> 00:28:47,119
one original copy

516
00:28:47,200 --> 00:28:48,119
and two duplicate copies.

517
00:28:48,319 --> 00:28:49,160
The sentencing is concluded.

518
00:28:49,359 --> 00:28:50,240
Please be seated.

519
00:28:53,799 --> 00:28:55,720
Bailiffs, please escort the defendant out.

520
00:29:20,319 --> 00:29:21,000
I'm heading out.

521
00:29:42,359 --> 00:29:43,079
Mr. Yu.

522
00:29:43,759 --> 00:29:44,440
Xiao Sun.

523
00:29:44,440 --> 00:29:45,119
Mr. Yu.

524
00:29:45,359 --> 00:29:46,359
Hello, hello.

525
00:29:46,359 --> 00:29:47,160
Mr. Yu.

526
00:29:47,240 --> 00:29:48,519
My first time...

527
00:29:48,599 --> 00:29:50,440
Having you at my first ever criminal trial

528
00:29:50,440 --> 00:29:51,559
means the world to me.

529
00:29:51,559 --> 00:29:51,920
Don't mention it.

530
00:29:51,920 --> 00:29:53,759
Keep it up. Keep working hard.

531
00:29:53,759 --> 00:29:54,960
Did I do okay today?

532
00:29:55,240 --> 00:29:56,640
You did. You did very well.

533
00:29:56,839 --> 00:29:57,599
Thank you, Mr. Yu.

534
00:29:57,720 --> 00:29:59,119
Let me buy you wontons tomorrow morning.

535
00:29:59,680 --> 00:30:00,960
Let's do it another time.

536
00:30:00,960 --> 00:30:02,960
I'm planning to take a trip soon.

537
00:30:02,960 --> 00:30:03,839
To get some rest.

538
00:30:03,920 --> 00:30:04,599
Then when you get back...

539
00:30:04,599 --> 00:30:05,519
give me a call.

540
00:30:05,519 --> 00:30:06,400
Okay, sure thing.

541
00:30:06,400 --> 00:30:06,799
Okay.

542
00:30:06,799 --> 00:30:07,880
Keep up the good work.

543
00:30:08,039 --> 00:30:09,000
Take care, Mr. Yu.

544
00:30:09,119 --> 00:30:10,000
Okay. Bye.

545
00:30:37,960 --> 00:30:39,119
Hello, I'm Lawyer Zhao.

546
00:30:39,119 --> 00:30:39,799
I know.

547
00:30:40,039 --> 00:30:40,759
Follow me.

548
00:31:22,319 --> 00:31:24,359
Lawyer Zhao, what's going on?

549
00:31:25,960 --> 00:31:26,839
Rujie Lecture Hall.

550
00:31:26,839 --> 00:31:29,559
Think of it as an internal study session.

551
00:31:29,680 --> 00:31:30,640
Don't take it too seriously.

552
00:31:31,440 --> 00:31:34,480
Treat it as a casual chat on any topic.

553
00:31:35,200 --> 00:31:36,119
I'm not asking you

554
00:31:36,119 --> 00:31:37,960
what kind of firm Rujie is.

555
00:31:37,960 --> 00:31:38,680
I mean,

556
00:31:39,559 --> 00:31:41,119
doing this leaves me totally unprepared.

557
00:31:41,279 --> 00:31:43,240
What's the point if you're prepared?

558
00:31:43,440 --> 00:31:45,359
You weren't prepared last night either.

559
00:31:45,519 --> 00:31:46,119
But...

560
00:31:46,240 --> 00:31:47,480
Alright, Ding Ning.

561
00:31:48,119 --> 00:31:48,920
I'm driving right now.

562
00:31:50,000 --> 00:31:51,240
Yang Awu is sick.

563
00:31:51,839 --> 00:31:53,599
He insists on having a hometown dish.

564
00:31:53,799 --> 00:31:55,720
I must pick up Yu Songfan for ingredients.

565
00:31:56,279 --> 00:31:57,119
So,

566
00:31:57,559 --> 00:31:59,680
handle the speech yourself, okay?

567
00:32:00,200 --> 00:32:00,920
Wait.

568
00:32:00,960 --> 00:32:02,079
You at least have to let me know

569
00:32:02,079 --> 00:32:04,160
who exactly is out there listening to me.

570
00:32:05,039 --> 00:32:05,759
Let me think...

571
00:32:05,920 --> 00:32:08,839
Most are interns from top law schools.

572
00:32:09,400 --> 00:32:10,079
And a few are

573
00:32:10,079 --> 00:32:12,039
litigators from international courts.

574
00:32:12,039 --> 00:32:12,559
Anyway,

575
00:32:12,559 --> 00:32:14,759
I had Xu Ruqing gather everyone available.

576
00:32:15,359 --> 00:32:16,559
Is it too late for me to leave?

577
00:32:16,799 --> 00:32:17,640
Oh, come on.

578
00:32:18,039 --> 00:32:20,039
I knew from the moment I met you

579
00:32:20,720 --> 00:32:22,039
that we're the same kind of person.

580
00:32:23,279 --> 00:32:24,200
You won't leave.

581
00:32:25,319 --> 00:32:26,400
You're just shy.

582
00:32:29,480 --> 00:32:30,039
I...

583
00:33:08,480 --> 00:33:10,079
Hello everyone, I'm Ding Ning.

584
00:33:15,559 --> 00:33:16,720
No profession

585
00:33:16,880 --> 00:33:18,839
feels more isolating than being a lawyer.

586
00:33:19,640 --> 00:33:21,920
We defend our clients time and time again.

587
00:33:22,359 --> 00:33:25,440
Even if the justice system is friendly,

588
00:33:25,839 --> 00:33:27,599
and public legal awareness is improving,

589
00:33:28,079 --> 00:33:29,319
the nature of our profession dictates that

590
00:33:29,319 --> 00:33:30,799
criminal defense lawyers must protect

591
00:33:30,799 --> 00:33:32,119
the legitimate rights of their clients,

592
00:33:32,759 --> 00:33:34,200
ensuring that all procedures

593
00:33:34,200 --> 00:33:35,759
and evidence are legal and valid.

594
00:33:36,759 --> 00:33:37,839
But in the eyes of the public,

595
00:33:38,440 --> 00:33:40,119
it's a job of speaking for lawbreakers

596
00:33:40,240 --> 00:33:41,079
and using that

597
00:33:41,839 --> 00:33:43,279
to collect money and make a living.

598
00:33:43,279 --> 00:33:44,279
How much hate we attract,

599
00:33:44,279 --> 00:33:45,640
I won't go into detail here.

600
00:33:48,839 --> 00:33:50,000
Over the past decade,

601
00:33:50,359 --> 00:33:52,160
there have been over 110

602
00:33:52,160 --> 00:33:53,559
defense lawyers sentenced to prison.

603
00:33:53,559 --> 00:33:55,200
The defense rate in criminal cases

604
00:33:55,200 --> 00:33:56,759
hovers around 30 percent.

605
00:33:56,880 --> 00:33:57,680
Now, let's look at the income.

606
00:33:58,240 --> 00:33:59,480
If you give up criminal law

607
00:33:59,480 --> 00:34:00,559
and instead take on,

608
00:34:01,279 --> 00:34:03,640
say, an IPO or M&A case,

609
00:34:03,799 --> 00:34:05,920
charging two to three million is common.

610
00:34:06,559 --> 00:34:09,280
But a criminal case only pays 30 to 50k.

611
00:34:09,280 --> 00:34:11,719
and even a major case is only 150k.

612
00:34:12,639 --> 00:34:14,760
So, why?

613
00:34:16,000 --> 00:34:18,000
Being a defense lawyer is a rational job,

614
00:34:18,199 --> 00:34:19,679
but when it comes to ourselves,

615
00:34:19,679 --> 00:34:21,199
we are so irrational.

616
00:34:21,960 --> 00:34:23,760
It doesn't make money, it's dangerous,

617
00:34:24,239 --> 00:34:25,519
and the environment is unfriendly.

618
00:34:25,920 --> 00:34:27,840
Yet we fight harder after every setback,

619
00:34:28,559 --> 00:34:30,000
brainwashing ourselves into thinking

620
00:34:30,000 --> 00:34:30,639
that this job

621
00:34:30,639 --> 00:34:32,880
has all sorts of social meaning and value.

622
00:34:33,239 --> 00:34:34,760
But more fundamentally,

623
00:34:35,280 --> 00:34:36,480
for ourselves,

624
00:34:37,079 --> 00:34:39,239
why do we do it?

625
00:34:43,000 --> 00:34:43,880
Before I spout

626
00:34:43,880 --> 00:34:45,559
some self-deceiving grand theories,

627
00:34:45,559 --> 00:34:47,199
let me introduce myself again.

628
00:34:47,800 --> 00:34:48,599
I work at a street-side law firm

629
00:34:48,599 --> 00:34:50,840
converted from a karaoke bar.

630
00:34:51,119 --> 00:34:53,320
Even a single meeting for a 200 yuan fee,

631
00:34:53,320 --> 00:34:54,519
I'll take that kind of job.

632
00:34:55,239 --> 00:34:56,960
My clients are usually

633
00:34:57,199 --> 00:34:58,440
delivery drivers pressured by orders,

634
00:34:58,760 --> 00:35:01,199
who snapped and smashed up a restaurant.

635
00:35:01,400 --> 00:35:02,440
Or unemployed women

636
00:35:02,440 --> 00:35:04,079
who became nannies to survive,

637
00:35:04,239 --> 00:35:05,000
but were sexually assaulted,

638
00:35:05,000 --> 00:35:07,320
and pushed the owner downstairs resisting.

639
00:35:07,320 --> 00:35:08,119
And so on.

640
00:35:09,079 --> 00:35:09,960
These are often

641
00:35:09,960 --> 00:35:11,679
the cases you wouldn't bother to take.

642
00:35:12,199 --> 00:35:14,679
But they're the soil I rely on to survive.

643
00:35:15,519 --> 00:35:16,320
So I guess

644
00:35:16,320 --> 00:35:17,880
Mr. Zhao Yijie invited me here

645
00:35:17,880 --> 00:35:18,639
not because

646
00:35:18,639 --> 00:35:20,400
I'm better at handling cases than you,

647
00:35:20,880 --> 00:35:23,119
but to use a bottom-tier lawyer like me

648
00:35:23,119 --> 00:35:25,559
to encourage you while spreading anxiety.

649
00:35:26,119 --> 00:35:27,880
But I personally really hate

650
00:35:27,880 --> 00:35:29,880
giving you all that kind of feeling.

651
00:35:30,159 --> 00:35:32,360
So let's not let him succeed, okay?

652
00:35:32,440 --> 00:35:33,199
Okay!

653
00:35:36,239 --> 00:35:38,079
All right, just a little chit-chat.

654
00:36:47,000 --> 00:36:47,840
What do you mean?

655
00:36:47,920 --> 00:36:49,440
Keep this out of the wind.

656
00:36:49,440 --> 00:36:50,800
It'll coagulate.

657
00:36:50,920 --> 00:36:53,039
You gotta keep stirring it. Hurry.

658
00:36:53,199 --> 00:36:54,000
How could...

659
00:36:54,239 --> 00:36:55,679
a kid this young...

660
00:36:55,679 --> 00:36:58,360
think of eating something so bloody?

661
00:36:58,559 --> 00:37:01,280
When kids get sick, they get homesick.

662
00:37:01,519 --> 00:37:04,039
Then they crave their hometown food.

663
00:37:04,239 --> 00:37:05,519
What's so weird about that?

664
00:37:05,719 --> 00:37:07,679
Didn't you see it just now?

665
00:37:07,679 --> 00:37:10,559
They just took a live pig,

666
00:37:10,960 --> 00:37:12,800
and from the cut... right here,

667
00:37:13,039 --> 00:37:15,280
the blood kept dripping into this basin.

668
00:37:15,280 --> 00:37:16,719
You think slaughtering a pig is cruel?

669
00:37:16,960 --> 00:37:17,599
Isn't it?

670
00:37:18,039 --> 00:37:19,599
Well, I don't see you being a vegetarian.

671
00:37:21,840 --> 00:37:23,239
It's just like some people,

672
00:37:23,440 --> 00:37:26,440
always saying how guilty they feel,

673
00:37:26,440 --> 00:37:29,199
yet they still went to Judge Sun

674
00:37:29,280 --> 00:37:30,480
to interfere with the verdict.

675
00:37:30,960 --> 00:37:32,079
That's why people

676
00:37:32,320 --> 00:37:34,519
are hypocritical with double standards.

677
00:37:34,679 --> 00:37:37,159
Is Alzheimer's contagious?

678
00:37:37,599 --> 00:37:38,800
Did I pass it on to you?

679
00:37:39,440 --> 00:37:40,559
Don't you remember?

680
00:37:40,800 --> 00:37:43,679
You told me to interfere with Judge Sun.

681
00:37:43,800 --> 00:37:45,199
If it weren't for my grandson,

682
00:37:45,400 --> 00:37:46,880
would I have done such a thing?

683
00:37:47,039 --> 00:37:48,599
Even with Alzheimer's, you didn't forget

684
00:37:48,599 --> 00:37:50,920
to get your grandson a paternity test.

685
00:37:52,000 --> 00:37:53,920
Don't pigs have a lot of parasites?

686
00:37:54,119 --> 00:37:55,599
There must be a ton in the blood.

687
00:37:55,599 --> 00:37:56,440
How can anyone eat this?

688
00:37:56,440 --> 00:37:57,599
Changing the subject

689
00:37:57,599 --> 00:37:59,920
means you're happy with the results.

690
00:38:05,880 --> 00:38:08,000
How's your Alzheimer's doing anyway?

691
00:38:08,360 --> 00:38:10,039
Do you still get ringing in your ears?

692
00:38:10,159 --> 00:38:11,960
Or you just can't remember numbers, right?

693
00:38:12,159 --> 00:38:13,679
Why do you care so much?

694
00:38:14,239 --> 00:38:15,480
Did you think of another dirty deed

695
00:38:15,480 --> 00:38:16,760
you want me to do for you?

696
00:38:19,159 --> 00:38:21,239
So even a judge like you

697
00:38:22,119 --> 00:38:23,800
can have professional prejudice.

698
00:38:23,880 --> 00:38:25,239
You always think we lawyers

699
00:38:25,239 --> 00:38:27,880
rely entirely on connections,

700
00:38:27,880 --> 00:38:29,920
and set traps to win cases, right?

701
00:38:29,920 --> 00:38:31,320
That we're all up to no good, right?

702
00:38:31,320 --> 00:38:32,000
Don't say that.

703
00:38:32,000 --> 00:38:33,440
I never said that.

704
00:38:33,519 --> 00:38:34,480
Not all lawyers.

705
00:38:34,480 --> 00:38:36,679
Just a lawyer like you.

706
00:38:37,079 --> 00:38:39,000
You're no stranger to breaking the law.

707
00:38:39,000 --> 00:38:40,400
Who framed Lao Kang?

708
00:38:40,400 --> 00:38:41,239
Should I give you a medal?

709
00:38:41,239 --> 00:38:43,159
Stop throwing the word "crimes" around.

710
00:38:43,280 --> 00:38:44,159
When it comes to Lao Kang,

711
00:38:44,159 --> 00:38:45,800
we're accomplices now.

712
00:38:45,920 --> 00:38:46,920
We're comrades-in-arms.

713
00:38:47,480 --> 00:38:49,599
Just like the butcher who killed the pig.

714
00:38:50,000 --> 00:38:51,480
The only difference between you and me is

715
00:38:51,480 --> 00:38:53,079
that you only dare to kill blindfolded.

716
00:38:53,440 --> 00:38:54,559
Who blindfolded me,

717
00:38:54,559 --> 00:38:57,239
and used my hand to kill the pig for him?

718
00:39:10,119 --> 00:39:11,280
Open your eyes right now!

719
00:40:08,800 --> 00:40:09,519
Grandpa.

720
00:40:11,760 --> 00:40:12,920
What's wrong with you?

721
00:40:16,840 --> 00:40:19,280
The pig blood you wanted spilled.

722
00:40:22,280 --> 00:40:23,400
There's nothing left to eat.

723
00:40:23,840 --> 00:40:25,800
Why do you want to eat such weird things?

724
00:40:26,119 --> 00:40:27,000
Tell me.

725
00:40:28,840 --> 00:40:29,400
Grandpa.

726
00:40:31,079 --> 00:40:31,639
Look.

727
00:40:32,519 --> 00:40:34,360
I finished drawing the wound.

728
00:40:37,880 --> 00:40:38,480
What?

729
00:40:39,079 --> 00:40:39,840
Lan.

730
00:40:42,159 --> 00:40:44,199
What does "Lan" mean?

731
00:40:46,159 --> 00:40:46,800
Home.

732
00:40:48,119 --> 00:40:51,000
We can see the tree friends when we go home.

733
00:40:57,320 --> 00:40:58,079
All right.

734
00:40:59,000 --> 00:41:00,440
Grandpa will take you home.

735
00:41:01,519 --> 00:41:04,079
To see your tree friends, okay?

736
00:41:13,880 --> 00:41:14,559
Let's go.

737
00:41:14,800 --> 00:41:15,239
Come on.

738
00:41:28,239 --> 00:41:28,880
Please continue.

739
00:41:33,119 --> 00:41:33,760
Mr. Xu.

740
00:41:37,599 --> 00:41:38,239
Mr. Zhao.

741
00:41:39,320 --> 00:41:40,119
Attorney Ding.

742
00:41:40,119 --> 00:41:40,440
You...

743
00:41:40,440 --> 00:41:42,199
really spoke brilliantly just now.

744
00:41:42,760 --> 00:41:43,519
I'm flattered.

745
00:41:44,599 --> 00:41:45,199
About those...

746
00:41:45,199 --> 00:41:46,920
can you send me those case files?

747
00:41:47,119 --> 00:41:48,960
Sure. I'll send you a copy later.

748
00:41:49,559 --> 00:41:50,360
If you have any questions later,

749
00:41:50,360 --> 00:41:51,199
feel free to contact me anytime.

750
00:41:59,599 --> 00:42:00,920
Congratulations on joining Rujie.
